  ▲ Missing format arguments
   ╭─[test.lis:5:11]
 4 │ fn main() {
 5 │   let _ = fmt.Errorf("bad %d: %w", 1)
   ·           ─────────────┬─────────────
   ·                        ╰── 2 verbs, 1 argument
 6 │ }
   ╰────
  help: `fmt.Errorf` has 2 verbs but 1 argument, so `%w` prints as `%!w(MISSING)`. Add the missing argument, remove the verb, or write `%%` for a literal percent sign · code: [lint.printf_verb_mismatch]
